The resampling kernels (bilinear, bicubic and three-lobe LANCZOS) in
se.alipsa.jmlx.vision are a Java port of Pillow's C resampling source, pinned at:

  Source file:  https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/blob/12.3.0/src/libImaging/Resample.c
  Source SHA-256: 808c212d03289b9ab70fad67168da1b14ed8dd74f1607c7a7278c50cbc1ae0ab

The alpha-compositing-over-white formula in ImageDecoder.compositeOverWhite is a Java port of
Pillow's alpha-composite source from the same pinned tag, which uses the SHIFTFORDIV255 macro
from the same tree's src/libImaging/ImagingUtils.h:

  Source file:  https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/blob/12.3.0/src/libImaging/AlphaComposite.c
  Source SHA-256: 0063c136b8bb2be51e2fb76fac222a7ae96b438f3c09706834862d9c1ac62c93

License file:   https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/blob/12.3.0/LICENSE
License SHA-256: 15181e7363dca9aed78b79bebebc7fde7f1814b8bd311ea3b87ae8ccadfc185b

The ported source files retain header comments naming the pinned source and its SHA-256, so the
carried code keeps the provenance independently of META-INF.

