The bicubic resize used by the Phi-3-vision processor (TorchBicubic in
se.alipsa.jmlx.vision) is a Java port of PyTorch's CPU upsampling source,
pinned at tag v2.6.0:

  Source file:  https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.6.0/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/UpSampleKernel.cpp
  Source SHA-256: e3b7bf13fecd1af33e1c6d7dfb441d97590b71075194d040c5ad325814fdac1f
  Source file:  https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.6.0/aten/src/ATen/native/UpSample.h
  Source SHA-256: d49801938b31a544d2f55d616eea5db4cbd611ba691dca128ccd6aa870d008ba

License file:   https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.6.0/LICENSE
License SHA-256: 47a26beb94e3f6b333a3677fc85d546f1fdfd2f0b3686c26d2fb5b10e0134165

The ported source retains a header comment naming the pinned sources and their SHA-256s, so the
carried code keeps the provenance independently of META-INF.

